<!-- eXplora 14x8 beech propeller. Xoar 14x8 (photo resources/explora_vtol_001.jpg shows the Xoar logo and the "14X8" stamp).
     C_THRUST / C_POWER: QPROP 1.22 velocity sweep at 6000 rpm,
     Ct = T/(rho n^2 D^4), Cp = Pshaft/(rho n^3 D^5), rho 1.225. Blade geometry:
     beta = atan(8 in / (2 pi r)) from the nominal pitch; chord = UIUC apce_14x12 c/R (no measured beech 14 in planform found);
     section polar = QPROP documentation set (CL0 0.5, CLmax 1.2), anchored on the UIUC apce_14x12 measured static Ct/Cp
     (-2.4 % / -7 %) and 3507 rpm sweep (-2.5 % / +8 %) with measured geometry, and on the T-Motor 14x4.8 bench (-8 % thrust).
     REGIME: at static / hover (J < 0.1) the blade sits at the CLmax clamp over its whole span (alpha ~7 deg at 0.75R), so
     Ct0 = 0.090 is set by CLmax x chord and is insensitive to pitch; CLmax 1.0 / 1.4 would move Ct0 -16 % / +9 %
     (polar sensitivity sweep). Validation vs the T-Motor MN4012 bench (CF 14x4.8 / 15x5): thrust -5..-12 %,
     electrical power -10..-23 %, so expect this table to be LOW by that order; see README.md. -->
